              {
                "id": 3528749,
                "postDate": "2026-09-26T11:46:00.320Z",
                "rawMarkdown": "It's not against the rules per se, it's just that our system isn't configured to run it. For one, we don't have the GPUs. The system is configured to accept LoRA adapters, so if you tried to submit it, the script would just throw an error. We chose to accept LoRA adapters to allow some amount of finetuning while also keeping submission file sizes moderate and for being more accessible under the hardware people are likely to have access to.",
                "content": "<p>It's not against the rules per se, it's just that our system isn't configured to run it. For one, we don't have the GPUs. The system is configured to accept LoRA adapters, so if you tried to submit it, the script would just throw an error. We chose to accept LoRA adapters to allow some amount of finetuning while also keeping submission file sizes moderate and for being more accessible under the hardware people are likely to have access to.</p>",
